Create a Python virtual environment named `ml-env` under /root/code/ and activate it:

```
python3 -m venv ml-env
source ml-env/bin/activate
```

The environment has numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, and matplotlib installed:

```
pip install numpy pandas scikit-learn matplotlib
```

To verify afterward:

```
pip list
```

Create a requirements.txt capturing the installed packages is saved at /root/code/requirements.txt

```
pip freeze > /root/code/requirements.txt
```
